# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DEPLOYMENT NOTES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Before deploying with this .env file:
#
# 1. SECURITY - Change ALL placeholder values:
#    - SECRET_KEY (generate new one):
#      python manage.py shell -c "from django.core.management.utils import get_random_secret_key; print(get_random_secret_key())"
#    - REDIS_PASSWORD (use strong password):
#      openssl rand -base64 32
#    - Update REDIS_URL, CACHE_LOCATION, CELERY_BROKER_URL, CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND with new REDIS_PASSWORD
#    - GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID & SECRET (confirm production OAuth app in Google Cloud Console)
#
# 2. ALLOWED_HOSTS - Add production server IP once known:
#    ALLOWED_HOSTS=...,<PRODUCTION_SERVER_IP>
#
# 3. PROJECT STRUCTURE:
#    - Project path: /var/www/html/kms
#    - Docker containers run within this directory
#    - Nginx reverse proxy configured to route kms.dpd.go.id → Docker containers
#
# 4. SSL/HTTPS:
#    - SSL certificates configured on nginx
#    - DEBUG=False with SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT=False (nginx handles SSL termination)
#    - Let's Encrypt certificates at: /etc/letsencrypt/live/kms.dpd.go.id/
#
# 5. DATABASE:
#    - PostgreSQL runs on host machine, accessed from Docker via host.docker.internal
#    - First deployment auto-runs migrations
#
# 6. GOOGLE OAUTH:
#    - Register https://kms.dpd.go.id/google/callback/ in Google Cloud Console
#    - Authorized redirect URIs must include this exact URL
#
# 7. VERIFICATION:
#    - Test: curl https://kms.dpd.go.id/api/v1/health/
#    - Admin: https://kms-be.dpd.go.id/admin/
#    - Verify no DEBUG errors exposed
#
# USAGE:
#   Copy this file to .env on the production server:
#   $ cp .env.production .env
#   $ docker-compose down && docker-compose up -d --build
